{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/334203-fixing-tempus-fugit","id":334203,"title":"Fixing Tempus Fugit","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-08T07:53:00-08:00","id":334203,"title":"Fixing Tempus Fugit","content":"So, I think that Pandemonium 5, <i>Tempus Fugit</i>, is too good. Like, brokenly too good. Granted, I say that about all abilities that grant multiple actions and believe that they're anathema to good game design*. So that should give you an idea of what I mean by &quot;fix&quot;.<br /> <br /> The non-combat use of it is fine, I think it's kind of neat. But I don't want to just rip out the combat application. I could shorten the duration of the effect to one round, which would make the cost prohibitive for all but the most important conflicts. However, that doesn't solve my core issues with the power (namely that it's <i>too good</i>). Instead I was thinking of changing it so that the user could choose where in the Initiative order they act for the rest of the turn, or give them a bonus to split dice pools.<br /> <br /> I doubt I'm the first person to have these problems, and was wondering what other people's workarounds were.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">*I am really not interested in discussing why I think that, nor will I bother responding to people asking: I just want y'all to understand where I'm coming from.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T17:40:38-08:00","id":334673,"title":"","content":"Not really sure why you would post an opinion and recommendation to fix something, and then not be interested in discussing why you may be wrong. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So, I completely disagree with you, and look forward to seeing Tempus Fugit Time Dilation/Contraction as is or more powerful than it was. Reasoning:<br /> <br /> It is a level 5 Arcanoi<br /> It it is a great thematic fit for Haunteurs and Pandemonium<br /> It fits thematically, and logically with tempest manipulation/fiddling<br /> It is the only way for wraiths to get multiple actions apart from Shadowplay<br /> Unless you're going to start removing Celerity, Time Sphere, Rage, etc... then it is not logically sound to call abilities that grant multiple actions broken or anathema to good game design, and proceed to fix them for only one subset - and the one that has the least access to that mechanic too!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4487-nerhesi","name":"Nerhesi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T17:57:02-08:00","id":334706,"title":"","content":"Multiple actions are only broken when the game they occur in relies on an action economy for it's balance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4449-eisenkreutzer","name":"EisenKreutzer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4449_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T19:02:30-08:00","id":334726,"title":"","content":"Despite saying that I didn't want to discuss it, I realize that my post came across as overly critical, based on y'all's responses. I don't want to sound like I'm criticising the game here, just a part of it that I think is, well, <i>bad</i>. Which is fine, lots of things that I like aren't perfect. <i>Pacific Rim</i>, <i>Majora's Mask</i>, and <i>Werewolf: The Forsaken, </i>for instance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nerhesi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/334203-fixing-tempus-fugit?p=334673#post334673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really sure why you would post an opinion and recommendation to fix something, and then not be interested in discussing why you may be wrong. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So, I completely disagree with you, and look forward to seeing Tempus Fugit Time Dilation/Contraction as is or more powerful than it was. Reasoning:<br /> <br /> <b>It is a level 5 Arcanoi<br /> ...</b><br /> <b>It is the only way for wraiths to get multiple actions apart from Shadowplay</b><br /> <b>Unless you're going to start removing Celerity, Time Sphere, Rage, etc... then it is not logically sound to call abilities that grant multiple actions broken or anathema to good game design, and proceed to fix them for only one subset - and the one that has the least access to that mechanic too!</b></div> </div> </div> </div>1) Yeah, but none of the others (in the core book) look as good to me. Obliviate is really good too, but it not only requires the investment every time you use it, it also pings you with Angst. So not only does it drain a resource, but it also hits you with an increasing negative aspect.<br /> <br /> 2) Shadowplay I'm still mulling over. It's not reliable for the player, and I'm a big fan of giving players enough rope to hang themselves with. Plus it's only <i>one</i> extra action, which seems reasonable every now and again, especially during a tense situation.<br /> <br /> 3) I'm not gonna be running any other cWoD games. I've only been looking at Wraith. I'd probably remove the multiple action abilities from the other games too, were I to run them! <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EisenKreutzer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/334203-fixing-tempus-fugit?p=334706#post334706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Multiple actions are only broken when the game they occur in relies on an action economy for it's balance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get that cWoD games don't rely on an action economy for balance, but I'm a fan of combat, and I don't like it when some of the players are engaged in a combat and some aren't. That's what I don't like about asymmetrical multiple action abilities like Tempus Fugit. I could let the Haunter dance all over my mooks, but everybody else has to sit back and just <i>watch</i>, which seems lame. Obviously I could throw an enemy with Tempus Fugit at them in return, but I don't feel like that fixes the problem since now there are <i>at least</i> two combatants at that point who are taking 50% of the turns.<br /> <br /> I hope this post helps clarify that I understand that my issues with Tempus Fugit are irrelevant to the designer's intent, but I'd still like some help fixing them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T20:15:28-08:00","id":334778,"title":"","content":"I think just making it so that is takes four turns to hit you is pretty damn mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T22:41:13-08:00","id":334839,"title":"","content":"Just switch the costs, so it's 4 Pathos and a Willpower instead of 2. Alternatively, have it last for a round rather than a scene. Or mix both; they'll quickly drain their Pathos reserves. <br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T01:22:13-08:00","id":334918,"title":"","content":"You can just erase this effect from the description. Tempus fugit is about contraction/dilatation of time as you said. Juste erase the line where it says that it gives multiple actions. It's optional to the power. <br /> <br /> Btw, I would myself make it more powerful for non combat situations : the capacity to change some minor things in the past for instance. And I would made it some kind of the goal of a chronicle for a specific time (a chronicle where you have to acquire that power, find the right haunt, convince him you have to learn it - or to do something for you).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/824-araknee","name":"Araknee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar824_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T16:56:07-08:00","id":335582,"title":"","content":"I'm of the mind that we need multiple actions, it shouldn't be something wraiths are not privvy too, and we need more powerful level 5 arcanoi. I want level 5 arcanoi to be &quot;wow! That is insane!&quot; the less so they are, the more easily you run into scenarios where there is only 1 or 2 good ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4487-nerhesi","name":"Nerhesi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T19:30:35-08:00","id":335693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nerhesi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/334203-fixing-tempus-fugit?p=335582#post335582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm of the mind that we need multiple actions, it shouldn't be something wraiths are not privvy too, and we need more powerful level 5 arcanoi. I want level 5 arcanoi to be &quot;wow! That is insane!&quot; the less so they are, the more easily you run into scenarios where there is only 1 or 2 good ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget that Arkanoi are easier to get than Disciplines for example. A wraith starts with 5 dots worth of Arkanoi, while a VAmpire starts with only 3 dots of Disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4449-eisenkreutzer","name":"EisenKreutzer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4449_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T20:49:52-08:00","id":335725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nerhesi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/334203-fixing-tempus-fugit?p=335582#post335582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm of the mind that we need multiple actions, it shouldn't be something wraiths are not privvy too, and we need more powerful level 5 arcanoi. I want level 5 arcanoi to be &quot;wow! That is insane!&quot; the less so they are, the more easily you run into scenarios where there is only 1 or 2 good ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that'll be for the Deadguy to figure out for W20. I'm willing to take the game as-is, I just need to fix what I think is one <i>glaring </i>flaw.<br /> <br /> I've been mulling over some fixes. I want Tempus Fugit to retain its <i>essence</i>, so to speak. The primary aspects of the ability that I want to keep are:<ul><li>Low cost</li> <li>Applicable in virtually every combat situation</li> <li>Always useful</li> <li>Doesn't allow for resistance</li> <li>Reliable</li> <li>Multiplicative bonus</li> </ul>The fact that it has all of these already makes it bonkers good to start with. All I need to do is fix the multiple actions part. To that end, my fix ideas:<br /> <br /> <b>System:</b> First paragraph as normal.<br /> This art costs 4 Pathos and 1 Willpower. Alternatively, by rolling <b>Dexterity (difficulty 7)</b>, a wraith my focus this art on himself alone, <b>decreasing the difficulty of all checks by the successes rolled for the rest of the scene</b>. This method costs 2 Pathos and 1 Willpower.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, I'm thinking about keeping with the theme of a bonus on splitting your actions to represent super-speed or whatever. Perhaps you may use the highest dice pool to calculate how many dice you have instead of the lowest dice pool when splitting actions? Could combine that with the fix above. Hmmm...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T12:58:37-08:00","id":336216,"title":"","content":"While I don't yet have experience playing Wraith, decreasing all difficulties seems even more broken. But then again I'm coming from Werewolf, where every PC gets several extra actions to use almost whenever they want per combat (as long as they find ways to refresh their rage), and difficulties are one of the limiting factors...it feels like doing some very difficult noncombat things require characters to research, get spiritual help, organize everything just right over a long period so they can lower difficulties into a more desirable range.<br /> <br /> Besides, if you are lucky and can lower your combat roll difficulty from 6 to like...3, then aren't your players going to be splitting their dice pools for multiple actions anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T14:36:22-08:00","id":336314,"title":"","content":"I'll admit I'm still not entirely happy with that implementation. Believe me, the first draft was uglier.<br /> <br /> - C.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Clayton A. Oliver | Formerly Ubiquitous<br /> <br /> <i>When the half-light starts to rise/And the long gone come back again<br /> After the shortcuts and the highs/Comes the pain<br /> And the rain</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2966-tegyrius","name":"Tegyrius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T08:43:06-08:00","id":337068,"title":"","content":"It's true that I'm not satisfied with the &quot;lower your difficulty by 0-5&quot;. Allowing splitting actions using the largest dice pool also introduces a weird quirk where you can be terrible at something but split your action with something you're good at and have <i>more</i> dice than you would for the thing you're bad at.<br /> <br /> Hmm...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T16:16:41-08:00","id":337477,"title":"","content":"No no no nono. This is a power that alters time; lowering the difficulty wouldn't get that feel. Besides, what if you wanted to do something simple, but really quickly, like run a distance? Then the difficulty lowering does nothing. As a haunter a good chunk of this power IS specifically for freaking people the fuck out; we shouldn't lose sight of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T18:51:57-08:00","id":337625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/334203-fixing-tempus-fugit?p=337477#post337477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No no no nono. This is a power that alters time; lowering the difficulty wouldn't get that feel. Besides, what if you wanted to do something simple, but really quickly, like run a distance? Then the difficulty lowering does nothing. As a haunter a good chunk of this power IS specifically for freaking people the fuck out; we shouldn't lose sight of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right. I'm gonna go back to the drawing board and instead of trying to simply alter Tempus Fugit I'll drop it entirely. Let's take a look at the rest of Pandemonium to see what's going on:<ul><li>Basic Ability: <b>Sense Chaos</b>. Simple, evocative. Gathers information of a specific type. Other Haunters about? What about Spectres? Useful</li> <li><b>Weirdness</b>: A straightforward power, this one. Do random ghost tricks, so that the audience knows that it's a ghost episode. It's fun.</li> <li><b>Befuddlement</b>: A really solid two-dot power, though not as versatile as it seems at first. For instance, you couldn't use it on targets in a group because they'd probably realize something is up, especially if any of them are Haunters. Open-ended, continues with the theme of &quot;weird, annoying&quot;.</li> <li><b>Dark Ether</b>: Basically a scarier version of <b>Weirdness</b> that's more expensive and may gain you some Angst. Affects an area rather than an individual, which is nifty.</li> <li><b>Foul Humor: </b>Powerful and in keeping with everything else. Affects an area with sick or vermin (or both). Does some light damage, though unlikely to bypass anybody's soak unless you roll stupid high. I really like this one.</li> </ul>So basically everything up until this part is kind of open-ended and emphasizes the theatrical nature of Haunters. The five-dot power should do that as well.<br /> <br /> At first I thought of animating the environment all around you, being able to fling objects around and the like, but that's getting into the Artificer's territory, I think. Maybe a one-ghost stage show, with smoke and lighting effects? Uncontrollable, area-wide chaos of some sort? A kind of Foul Humor++?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T11:20:25-08:00","id":341008,"title":"","content":"I recently rewatched <i>Beetlejuice</i> (thanks Wraith Players Guide). Decided to take a look at my <i>Geist</i> books as well to see if there was something I could backport into <i>Wraith</i>, and the Boneyard Manifestation and the Phantasmal Key stood out as appropriate for Pandemonium.<br /> <br /> To that end, I have a new idea about what Pandemonium 5 should look like:<br /> <br /> <b><u>Tempestas Mortuorum </u></b>(sorry for the Google Latin translation, I assume somebody will school me about what this should be)<br /> The Haunter assumes control over the immediate area. The ground, the air, the water, everything that isn't infused with a Soul becomes the user's plaything. It is the ultimate expression of Pandemonium: reality itself bends its knee to madness. Structures and objects made of Soulsteel are not affected. However, the power works regardless of the environment: The Skinlands, the Tempest, and the Shadowlands are all fair game.<br /> <b>System</b>: The Haunter rolls Intelligence+Pandemonium (difficulty 7). For every success, the area of effect of Temepestas Mortuorum is 100 yards from the user. Within this area, the wraith has near-complete control over the environment. She can stretch hallways or make them shorter, she can make doors appear or disappear, flatten stairwells so that they're smooth ramps, or change the temperature. This costs 3 Pathos and 1 Willpower and lasts for the scene.<br /> The Wraith may also directly attack targets using the environment. She does not need to see the target, they merely have to be within the area. The attacks take the form of the environment twisting to hinder and damage the target. Perhaps the rungs of a ladder disappear while the target is trying to climb them, or the ground twists and turns under their feet, or strips of wallpaper that try to strangle and constrict.<br /> Attacks are resolved as normal, using Dexterity+Pandemonium, but the Wraith gains 3 Angst if they use Tempestas Mortuorum in this fashion.<br /> <br /> This is a first draft, and I don't have the book with me to double-check some of the base systems, but this is where I'm headed right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T12:58:49-08:00","id":344039,"title":"","content":"After rereading the book, especially the rules regarding Willpower, I'm thinking the cost of Tempestas Mortuorum is too high, especially regarding Angst and Willpower. I'd remove the Willpower cost for both uses, and reduce the Angst gain to 1. However, I'd also add a couple of constraints and clarifications to the first use:<br /> <br /> <b>System</b>: The Haunter rolls Intelligence+Pandemonium (difficulty 7). For every success, the area of effect of Temepestas Mortuorum is <b>10 yards </b>from the user. Within this area, the wraith has near-complete control over the environment. She can stretch hallways or make them shorter, flatten stairwells so that they're smooth ramps, or adjust the temperature. This costs 3 Pathos and lasts for the scene. <b>The Haunter may not destroy objects. Walls must be left intact, though they can be weakened. </b><b>Changes to the environment persist, useful for large-scale remodeling and redecorating.</b><br /> The Wraith may also directly attack targets using the environment. She does not need to see the target, they merely have to be within the area. The attacks take the form of the environment twisting to hinder and damage the target. Perhaps the rungs of a ladder disappear while the target is trying to climb them, or a dark maw opens up in the ground under their feet, or strips of wallpaper that try to strangle and constrict. Let your imagination run wild, respecting the usual constraints.<br /> Attacks are resolved as normal, using Dexterity+Pandemonium, but the Wraith gains <b>1 Angst </b>if they use Tempestas Mortuorum in this fashion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T12:29:45-07:00","id":446375,"title":"","content":"The latter version sounds more balanced. I like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}